// Optional tile sections alongside freely positioned entities.
// Run: Appeal.exe Examples/World/Tile_Map_Sections
Run Setup/Config
World Create Tile_Demo
World Create_Typed_Entity Rock Rock 1 1
World Create_Typed_Entity Door Door 1 0
World Create_Entity Player
World Set_Position Player 3.5 2.25 0

World Create_Section Entrance 8 6
World Create_Section Forest 8 6
World Set_Tile_Size Entrance 32 32 1
World Set_Tile_Size Forest 32 32 1
World Set_Tile Entrance 0 0 Rock
World Set_Tile Entrance 1 0 Rock
World Set_Tile Entrance 7 1 Door
World Set_Tile Forest 0 0 Rock
World Connect_Sections Entrance Right Forest
World Set_Door_Destination Door Forest 32 32 0
World Use_Section Entrance

// Save writes each type list and each named section separately.
World Save Tile_Demo
World Close_Scene Tile_Demo
World Load Tile_Demo
Print (World Get_Tile Entrance 1 0 Type)
Print (World Get_Tile Entrance 1 0 ID)
Print (World Get_Neighbor Entrance Right)
Print (World Get_Door_Destination Door)
// World Draw emits placements to an installed native Entity_Renderer callback.
// A game renderer can also query Get_Tile Name/X/Y/Z without moving prototypes.
Done
